00:55:41.550 --> 00:55:43.350
I never ask anything of you.

1273
00:55:44.030 --> 00:55:44.890
Dwight enters.

1274
00:55:45.570 --> 00:55:46.790
Dwight says, my desk.

1275
00:55:47.010 --> 00:55:49.410
Michael says, oh yeah, you should move back here.

1276
00:55:49.750 --> 00:55:51.090
Jim goes, damn it.

1277
00:55:51.750 --> 00:55:53.550
Dwight gives Michael a huge hug.

1278
00:55:53.770 --> 00:55:55.310
Pam says, it's okay, honey.

1279
00:55:55.490 --> 00:55:58.250
I told you not to let yourself believe it could happen.

1280
00:55:59.790 --> 00:56:01.350
Dwight kisses his desk.

1281
00:56:01.350 --> 00:56:02.530
It's kind of sweet.

1282
00:56:02.710 --> 00:56:07.810
And then he takes out a large knife and starts immediately carving his own name into the desk.

1283
00:56:08.610 --> 00:56:10.210
Michael says, glad you're back.

1284
00:56:10.770 --> 00:56:10.930
Aw.

1285
00:56:11.430 --> 00:56:13.710
Jim had his moment, but it didn't happen.

1286
00:56:15.010 --> 00:56:19.670
Well, listen, Pam and Andy managed to destroy Andy's computer enough.

1287
00:56:19.910 --> 00:56:21.550
Oh yeah, they put all kinds of stuff in it.

1288
00:56:21.610 --> 00:56:23.890
Bologna, mustard, scratched it up.

1289
00:56:24.090 --> 00:56:24.510
Yes.

1290
00:56:24.850 --> 00:56:27.010
And she has replaced it.

1291
00:56:27.250 --> 00:56:35.830
But then they have to kind of scuff up the new one so that she can convince everyone that she found it on a shelf in the warehouse somewhere.

1292
00:56:36.130 --> 00:56:36.250
Mm-hmm.

1293
00:56:36.930 --> 00:56:39.310
This makes Daryl's ears perk up.

1294
00:56:39.650 --> 00:56:41.210
He's like, you found it in the warehouse, huh?

1295
00:56:41.410 --> 00:56:41.850
Mm-hmm.

1296
00:56:41.850 --> 00:56:41.990
Mm-hmm.

1297
00:56:42.210 --> 00:56:42.510
Yeah.

1298
00:56:43.010 --> 00:56:45.130
So Daryl approaches Pam in the break room.

1299
00:56:45.250 --> 00:56:46.950
He's going to call bullshit on that.

1300
00:56:47.070 --> 00:56:48.070
He sure is.

1301
00:56:48.070 --> 00:56:50.390
I'm calling this scene bullshit in the break room.

1302
00:56:50.590 --> 00:56:56.490
He says maybe she should go back down there and find him some extra sick days on a shelf somewhere.

1303
00:56:57.230 --> 00:56:57.750
Scandalous.

1304
00:56:58.570 --> 00:56:59.350
And you know what?

1305
00:56:59.430 --> 00:57:03.250
She does remember seeing a sick day on the shelf.

1306
00:57:03.550 --> 00:57:03.850
Five.

1307
00:57:04.410 --> 00:57:06.010
Yeah, Daryl remembers five.

1308
00:57:06.230 --> 00:57:06.490
Mm-hmm.

1309
00:57:06.650 --> 00:57:07.550
Pam says three.

1310
00:57:08.110 --> 00:57:08.610
Agreed.

1311
00:57:08.910 --> 00:57:10.830
We had a fan question from Amanda A.

1312
00:57:10.890 --> 00:57:11.570
in North Carolina.

1313
00:57:11.850 --> 00:57:17.610
Who said in the tag when Daryl asked Pam if she can find him some extra sick days, how would this work?

1314
00:57:18.010 --> 00:57:20.590
Is this really something Pam would have control over?

1315
00:57:20.890 --> 00:57:24.430
Apparently Pam has a lot more control than we could ever imagine.

1316
00:57:24.430 --> 00:57:25.610
She can get computers.

1317
00:57:25.810 --> 00:57:27.070
She can fudge the system.

1318
00:57:27.330 --> 00:57:28.190
That's what I'm saying.

1319
00:57:28.190 --> 00:57:31.350
Who was in charge of all of this before she had this job?

1320
00:57:31.510 --> 00:57:32.210
Who did this?

1321
00:57:32.330 --> 00:57:33.930
Was it supposed to be Michael?

1322
00:57:34.310 --> 00:57:34.730
Yes.

1323
00:57:34.730 --> 00:57:39.750
Is this stuff that she used to do as the receptionist and Michael would just kind of sign off on it?

1324
00:57:39.890 --> 00:57:42.050
I think she did a lot of Michael's job.

1325
00:57:42.150 --> 00:57:44.410
And so she knew how to manipulate the system.

1326
00:57:44.530 --> 00:57:45.490
That's what I think.

1327
00:57:46.090 --> 00:57:50.930
You know, in her final talking head, Pam says she's full-on corrupt.

1328
00:57:51.210 --> 00:57:51.470
Mm-hmm.

1329
00:57:51.570 --> 00:57:53.070
And she's delighted by it.

1330
00:57:53.070 --> 00:57:54.430
But here's my question.

1331
00:57:55.130 --> 00:57:57.370
What is Pam getting out of this deal?

1332
00:57:57.750 --> 00:57:58.950
Why is she corrupt?

1333
00:57:59.350 --> 00:58:00.250
What did she get?

1334
00:58:00.570 --> 00:58:04.830
I know she manipulated the system, but it was in Andy's favor.

1335
00:58:05.210 --> 00:58:11.030
And then I guess she's corrupt because she's covering up what she did by giving a favor to another person.

1336
00:58:11.430 --> 00:58:15.010
I'm not understanding what's in it for Pam.

1337
00:58:15.370 --> 00:58:16.950
She gets to hold power.

1338
00:58:17.210 --> 00:58:19.010
The power's gone to her head.

1339
00:58:19.190 --> 00:58:21.210
And now she's part of a cover-up.

1340
00:58:21.210 --> 00:58:22.670
I guess that's what it is.

1341
00:58:23.530 --> 00:58:25.970
Well, guys, that was Todd Packer.

1342
00:58:26.270 --> 00:58:27.590
We hope you enjoyed.

1343
00:58:27.990 --> 00:58:30.250
Maybe get yourself some tasty cakes.

1344
00:58:30.250 --> 00:58:31.270
We sure like them.

1345
00:58:31.350 --> 00:58:32.590
Or maybe an ant farm.

1346
00:58:32.870 --> 00:58:35.650
Yeah, or go buy yourself a Justice Beaver shirt.

1347
00:58:36.050 --> 00:58:38.830
We will be back next week with garage sale.

1348
00:58:39.070 --> 00:58:40.150
Oh, my goodness.

1349
00:58:40.790 --> 00:58:42.690
We have a lot to share about that one.

1350
00:58:43.030 --> 00:58:44.490
Have a great week, you guys.

1351
00:58:44.750 --> 00:58:46.670
And I have something for you guys as we go.

1352
00:58:46.830 --> 00:58:47.090
What?

1353
00:58:47.210 --> 00:58:47.810
What is it?

1354
00:58:48.910 --> 00:58:50.390
Come on, everybody.

1355
00:58:50.390 --> 00:58:51.230
What is this?

1356
00:58:51.410 --> 00:58:54.950
It's the Bowling Alley song from Grease 2, Angela.

1357
00:58:55.410 --> 00:58:57.210
I have not seen this.

1358
00:58:57.430 --> 00:58:59.250
The song is called Score Tonight.

1359
00:58:59.470 --> 00:58:59.990
That's right.

1360
00:59:00.110 --> 00:59:01.050
Do you get it?

1361
00:59:01.230 --> 00:59:03.110
It's a double entendre.

1362
00:59:03.110 --> 00:59:08.140
Oh, this gets four dongs up.

1363
00:59:08.540 --> 00:59:10.280
It sure does.

